</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>The aging physician: Changes in cognitive processing and their impact on medical practice.</article-title><source>Academic Medicine</source><volume>71</volume><fpage>S1</fpage><lpage>S6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12377689</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list><fn-group><fn fn-type="conflict"><p><bold>Competing Interests: </bold>The authors have declared that no competing interests exist.</p></fn><fn fn-type="financial-disclosure"><p><bold>Funding: </bold>This research was supported by the Academic Development Fund (ADF) of the University of Western Ontario, grant #R3507A04 to JPM. <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.uwo.ca/research/rds/internal/rds_funding_internfunding_researchgrants_newresearch.html">http://www.uwo.ca/research/rds/internal/rds_funding_internfunding_researchgrants_newresearch.html</ext-link> The funders had no role in study design, data collection and analysis, decision to publish, or preparation of the manuscript.</p></fn></fn-group></back></article>